2026-09-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2255) 'The public address is IPv6 only, and it is untested from this desk: WSL here has no IPv6 route.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2255) 'What it costs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2255) 'A redeploy restarts Bao, and Bao comes back sealed; the rollout that shipped this needed one unseal. The image rebuild also re-clones the OpenBao fork at its branch head, so a rebuild for sshd can change the Bao binary too. The public 8200 service is gone from `fly.toml`, so the only public port is 2222.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2255) 'The host key sits on the data volume and survives a redeploy. Its fingerprint is `SHA256:6xkNw5/8n/fRVyYU9SC0/ON+qRh+WSfVCYp8CCeuaXg`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2255) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2255) 'Every other route in use was an operator-held proxy, which is a person, not a path.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2255  1 LINE
 Text:Written
